# Line endings: one rule for every platform, independent of anyone's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# Git for Windows' installer sets `core.autocrlf=true` in the *system* config, so a fresh Windows
# clone rewrites every tracked file to CRLF in the working tree. Git stores LF, so `git status`
# stays clean and nothing looks wrong — but `pnpm lint` (`biome check .`, whose formatter wants LF)
# then reports a format error for every file, and the obvious reaction, `biome check --write`,
# rewrites the whole repository. That cost a CI cycle once (issue #61).
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the index when a file is committed; `eol=lf` checks LF out on
# every platform. The index already stores LF for all 263 text files, so this rule changes no
# committed content — it only pins what the working tree looks like from now on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# `text=auto` decides by content, and a binary that happens to look like text would be normalised
# and corrupted. These are the types this repository carries or could plausibly gain.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
*.sqlite binary
